# Binary payloads must never be line-ending translated.
#
# The repository had no .gitattributes at all, so git fell back to its content
# heuristic: a file with no NUL bytes near the start is treated as text. Five of
# the six committed PDFs are small enough to be misclassified that way, so with
# core.autocrlf=true - the default on Windows, including the GitHub hosted
# runners - every checkout rewrote LF to CRLF inside them and corrupted them.
#
# The visible symptoms were a fidelity manifest hash that drifted only in CI
# (CorpusSmokeTests.Corpus_commit_matches_the_pinned_manifest_hash), and MuPDF
# logging "cannot recognize xref format / trying to repair broken xref" for
# every corpus document in the hosted render proof but never locally.
#
# Marking these binary pins the checked-out bytes to the committed blob on every
# platform. Add any new binary format here rather than relying on the heuristic.

*.pdf   binary
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.bmp   binary
*.ttf   binary
*.otf   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.dll   binary
*.exe   binary
*.pdb   binary
*.lib   binary
*.so    binary
*.dylib binary
*.zip   binary
*.gz    binary
*.tar   binary
*.7z    binary
*.pfx   binary
*.snk   binary
*.traineddata binary
